{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155727-choosing-a-city-for-a-chronicles-of-darkness-game","id":1155727,"title":"Choosing a city for a Chronicles of Darkness game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-04T07:53:05-07:00","id":1155727,"title":"Choosing a city for a Chronicles of Darkness game.","content":"So I'm preparing and setting up for running a Changeling game. Trying to get everything ready, and I'm trying to figure out what city to set this in. Cities have a spirit of their own and a attitude that they cast upon the story.<br /> <br /> For example my Home town Waukesha, WI is home to Generac the Generator Manufacture, lots of wooded/forested areas, and very close to Milwaukee and home of the Engine plant for Harley Davidson. I tend to state that Milwaukee was the capital of a massive Werewolf Protectorate. But I for example would see a high number of the fan splat genius coming out of Waukesha/Milwaukee particularly since Briggs &amp; Stratton's generators, Kohler, and Generac are all out of Wisconsin it seems like Genius or a lot of Promethean would be coming out of here.<br /> <br /> But I'm looking for a city for this changeling game to base this theme around. &quot;You will never be fixed, but you can be better.&quot; With the sub theme of &quot;You are what you make of yourself.&quot;<br /> <br /> I had first though New Orleans but the &quot;City of Second Chances&quot; might be too hopeful.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to Salt Lake City - A city founded on hope, a chance for a new life, and to start anew away from enemies. This seems good...but still might be a bit too cheery, too optimistic. I could see this as a city with a high population of Fan Splat Princess: The Hopeful (Vocational). Yet all that hope is juxtaposed by the influx of people areas where there is a high rate of unemployment and joblessness(Great again for Promethean), while this does create an environment that would work good for some games, I doubt it works for what I am intending. I doubt this one works too.<br /> <br /> Chicago is also close to me, but...when I think Chicago in the Chronicles of Darkness I think a city under a mobster vampire rule. Where other supernaturals are forced to submit and provide protection offerings (blood dolls, money, magic) to the Vampires, in particular the faction of vampires who controls their section of the city. This might be a bit too hopeless...<br /> <br /> You can see my frustration. I need help picking a good city.<br /> <br /> Can you sell me one? Help me pick?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T09:41:08-07:00","id":1155756,"title":"","content":"So I've managed to Narrow things down and two cities I had decided against are now the top running cities. I could use some help laying out the supernatural scenes in these cities though.<br /> New Orleans - I'm thinking High Presence of Mages, Vampires, and Changelings. With the strongest presence of Bokur in the continental United States. Changelings are drawn to the city for it's contract of second chances. What would the hedge here look like? What areas would be the strongest? Which would be the weakest? How likely are the conflicts between supernaturals? How likely are political alliances? Who would side with whom? What kind of courts would have the strongest purchase here?<br /> <br /> Salt Lake City - Hopeful, Promethean, Demon? So what would draw Changelings here? Is it the hope? The Stories? Something else? Have I picked the right Supernaturals? What would the Hedge here be like? How would supernatural politics play out? Who has the strongest presence here? What kind of courts would thrive here? Also how to make this good for my players without being biased?<br /> <br /> Somewhere between Chicago and Milwaukee - With Chicago controlled by vampires and Milwaukee controlled by the werewolves and a cold war between the two simply because neither side thinks they could win and keep control of the other's territory, a story about someone trying to heat up that cold war into total war might be a fun plot for the character's to be caught in, but a very hard and complexed one to run. What kind of court could survive in a area where they are either bending the knee and making oaths of loyalty to the werewolves, and forced to join the hunts maybe as expendable mercenaries, or in Chicago where they are offering up members or humans, or hedge crafted magic in order to not be wiped out as dinner?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T14:12:39-07:00","id":1155852,"title":"","content":"A good way to get a grip on a place is to start looking up tourist attractions and popular spots. One method I use to help is google maps and start slapping points down on places of interest, then propping them up into a structure as I go along. I just thought up some New Orleans stuff in the spoiler down below, as for Salt Lake city, I'm at a loss for ideas. For the Claw vs Fang idea, maybe two courts, like the Dusk and Dawn courts, except one sides with the Wolves and the other with the Vamps, and ruling the area is based on a duel between the strongest between them. Or maybe a game of catpaws and cunning to bring ruin upon the current ruler of the Freehold for the crown?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> For N'Orleans, The Hedge is probably more colorful than in other places, tinted pink and purples and greens from the party going on in the mortal realm. Thorns of broken beer bottles and vines made out of Mardi Gras beads mark the paths, and strange goblin fruits grow from beer-sap trees and the beer-and-piss smell from the French Quarter is present at all times. The powers of Faerie are strong in the French Quarter, where the Glamour never runs dry, and the Frenchman Art Market, where the dreams of man find their way to the canvas and notes of the artists of Louisiana. The Big Easy could have have the Seasonal Courts, each one trading not with the seasons of man, but the year. In New Orleans, all courts are defined by their parties - a Spring Mardi Gras may be everything you've ever fantasized about, stretching into the long hours of the night, screaming in ectasy, but a Summer Mardi Gras is a wild gathering, like a meetup from every frat-bro and muscle-head, erupting in drunken brawls. Autumn parties are somber affairs, resembling two business men meeting for a drink, then trading information as the alcohol goes down, while Winter balls are masquerades, no attendee allowed to show their face, and the entire get-together hidden away from prying eyes, or maybe even hidden in plain sight.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps these Lost have made their own courts: Courts of Drinks, Beads, Masks, and Death. The Court of Drinks seek to drink themselves until they die, ambitious thrill-seekers and daring adventurers all in one, hoping that for all their bravado, they can out think, out act, and outplay the Fair Folk by the skin of their asses. Meanwhile, the Court of Beads keep to their studios and workshops, all of them artisans, musicians, and craftsmen, all tiring over canvas and forge, hoping that they can get it right, the token or contract that will repel Keepers forevermore. Hidden away are the Courts of Masks, information brokers and drug dealers, calling them a court of lawbreakers wouldn't be wrong, but it wouldn't be correct either; they hold promises deeply, like all Lost, but in New Orleans, the Masks are most likely to find loopholes and follow wordings to-the-letter. Finally, the Court of Death stands alone in the graves and mausoleums of the Big Easy, attracted to the death and despair New Orleans brings upon the mortals; Vampires run rampant in the city, and the body count keeps these Lost in business. Whereas the Masks learn and sell, the Beads create and understand, and the Drinks seek and defeat, the Death court destroys and hides. They keep the secrets in New Orleans secret. Mask courtiers would sell anything they know, hawk any item they find, but the Death courtiers would sooner see token destroyed than give them to another Changeling. The ruling period of New Orleans both begins, and finishes on Mardi Gras, with the most impressive display crowning someone ruler of the Freehold.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19270-princevertigo","name":"PrinceVertigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19270_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T14:21:52-07:00","id":1155853,"title":"","content":"You can always use my write up of Savannah, all the charm of New Orleans, with even more rot and corruption behind it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T15:23:00-07:00","id":1155878,"title":"","content":"Saying that Chicago is going to be about mobsters is like saying Portland would be about getting Shanghai\u2019d. Look to modern events and strange happenings, not whatever was going on a century ago for a brief decade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T17:29:47-07:00","id":1155896,"title":"","content":"I've always wanted to cook up something with Seoul as a Changeling setting. The name &quot;Seoul&quot; comes from archaic Korean for &quot;iron fence&quot; or &quot;iron hedge,&quot; so there's clearly something to be explored here with regards to the Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T19:35:30-07:00","id":1155919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155727-choosing-a-city-for-a-chronicles-of-darkness-game?p=1155878#post1155878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying that Chicago is going to be about mobsters is like saying Portland would be about getting Shanghai\u2019d. Look to modern events and strange happenings, not whatever was going on a century ago for a brief decade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chicago is also about vampires. And Vampires are not about &quot;getting with the times&quot; or &quot;What is current&quot; they are about holding on to things far longer than they should be. Keeping old traditions until all meaning behind them is lost, and clinging to the glorious past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T19:52:08-07:00","id":1155921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155727-choosing-a-city-for-a-chronicles-of-darkness-game?p=1155919#post1155919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chicago is also about vampires. And Vampires are not about &amp;quot;getting with the times&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;What is current&amp;quot; they are about holding on to things far longer than they should be. Keeping old traditions until all meaning behind them is lost, and clinging to the glorious past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chicago is also about Werewolves and Mages, if we\u2019re going off canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T21:08:53-07:00","id":1155937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155727-choosing-a-city-for-a-chronicles-of-darkness-game?p=1155921#post1155921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chicago is also about Werewolves and Mages, if we\u2019re going off canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I moved the Werewolves to Milwaukee, where they belong. Any werewolves still living in Chicago serve the vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T21:44:22-07:00","id":1155943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155727-choosing-a-city-for-a-chronicles-of-darkness-game?p=1155937#post1155937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I moved the Werewolves to Milwaukee, where they belong. Any werewolves still living in Chicago serve the vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, and we were supposed to know that how...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T01:34:02-08:00","id":1155980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155727-choosing-a-city-for-a-chronicles-of-darkness-game?p=1155943#post1155943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, and we were supposed to know that how...?</div> </div> </div> </div>The second post, where I describe Chicago as Vampire Controlled, and needing to survive by offering up blood donors, magic, or services to survive. This would indicate a strangle hold level of control over the people who live there. Plus there was the way I described surviving in Milwaukee in the second post, and the is a cold war between the two cities because of the controlling supernatural parties. Of course if you like I could elaborate further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T03:47:57-08:00","id":1155996,"title":"","content":"So a halfway point would be Waukegan and Kenosha?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T06:08:45-08:00","id":1156026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155727-choosing-a-city-for-a-chronicles-of-darkness-game?p=1155996#post1155996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a halfway point would be Waukegan and Kenosha?</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely yes. Maybe Lake Zurich","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T17:03:15-08:00","id":1161008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155727-choosing-a-city-for-a-chronicles-of-darkness-game#post1155727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can see my frustration. I need help picking a good city.<br /> <br /> Can you sell me one? Help me pick?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would respectfully suggest that you might be &quot;flattening&quot; these options a bit. By which I mean, taking the most prominent or well-publicized aspect of a city and taking it as representative of the whole. To be clear, my point here isn't about &quot;realism&quot; (although that applies to if you care about that) but about making a sufficiently complex environment for players to interact with.<br /> <br /> There's another way to do this, which is to select a city <i>semi</i>-randomly, and then research the ever-living crap out of it. Read up on its history, start keeping an eye on the local media, use googlemaps streetview to &quot;explore&quot;. What almost invariably happens (to me, anyway) is that the incomparable richness of the real world starts giving me ideas and opportunities that I never would have considered otherwise. For example, I'm currently working on developing Austin, TX as a setting for a CtL game. I picked it on the basis of its reputation for &quot;weirdness&quot;, but didn't know that it's sitting right next to a massive limestone formation that is absolutely riddled with caves and caverns, some of them containing weird species of spiders and fish that are found nowhere else in the world. Or that America's first ever serial killer was active there. Or that it's the only city in the world that still has functioning &quot;moonlight towers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Salt Lake City has its origin myth and everything, <a href=\"http://www.good4utah.com/good4utah/salt-lake-considered-a-hub-for-cartels-selling-mexican-meth/212004452\" target=\"_blank\">but it's also a major hub for the Sinaloa Cartel's meth trade</a>. That's a barrel of story hooks right there.<br /> <br /> I find a somewhat stochastic method for making these decisions worthwhile, because it encapsulates what's great about storytelling games that use dice instead of fiat: stuff happens that you would never have decided on, but is actually way cooler than what you would have chosen. The theme of &quot;trying to get better&quot; puts me in mind of sanatoriums and the self-help/wellness culture in America. I just did about 4 minutes of research and found out that the Southwest was a major center of sanatoria during the tuberculosis epidemic of the 19th century, and Tucson was the epicenter. Later on, it served as a center of rehabilitation for WWI veterans who had suffered mustard gas attacks. That's pure story hook gold there.<br /> It's also the site of a big airforce base that serves as the &quot;boneyard&quot; for all of the Air Force's excess, out-of-service aircraft. Miles of B-52s baking away in the Arizona sun...<br /> Completely unrelated, it's home to &quot;A Mountain&quot;, so-called because of a gigantic letter A on its side in honor of the University of Arizona. Not that interesting, until you find out that around the time of the Iraq War, there was an ongoing battle between students (who would traditionally whitewash it regularly) and anti-war activists (who painted it black in protest of the war). Something about this strikes me as very &quot;changeling-y&quot;. Maybe not your cup of tea, but the point is that I got that out of about 5 minutes of research.<br /> <br /> Explore, learn, and get invested in the details- it'll pay off come game time!<br /> <br /> (Side note: I personally try to stay away from the huge metropolises. As population/size increase linearly, the complexity of the whole increases exponentially, and it can be hard to do justice to a city of several million with a huge range of neighborhoods and other subdivisions. Cities of a couple hundred thousand work better for me- YMMV, of course.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155727-choosing-a-city-for-a-chronicles-of-darkness-game?p=1155919#post1155919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chicago is also about vampires. And Vampires are not about &quot;getting with the times&quot; or &quot;What is current&quot; they are about holding on to things far longer than they should be. Keeping old traditions until all meaning behind them is lost, and clinging to the glorious past.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true, but the Prohibition period was a bit of a flash in the pan in the kind of timescales that vampires deal in- while certainly it would make sense that there would be a certain cohort of licks who were drawing on that era and that subculture, I think they'd make more sense as a bloc than a representative of the whole. And there's something cool about having a gang of dead wisguys having a standoff with elders who were embraced when cowboys were still making massive cattle drives all the way from Texas to Chicago. Variety being the spice of unlife and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":22980,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22980-robothedino","user":"robothedino","date":". 11-20-2017, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22980-robothedino","name":"robothedino","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T18:37:54-08:00","id":1161033,"title":"","content":"Any city, with a bit of a spin, could be fun for CoD. It's all a matter of emphasis and style. I ran a fun Changeling campaign in Minneapolis; I've always wanted to set one in Kansas City ... two states, multiple jurisdictions, not quite Southern, not quite Western, very betwixt and between. <br /> <br /> My players want my next game to be set in Las Vegas, so I will oblige them, but I am not concentrating on The Strip, but opening it up to a wider template ... lost Anasazi, nuclear tests, the strange origins of the Rancho (before it became a city), and the interplay between a huge metro region sitting in the middle of the Mojave.<br /> <br /> Take any city. Look into its history. Give it a twist. Have some fun \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T20:57:35-08:00","id":1161072,"title":"","content":"I think It is time...I admit to my deception.<br /> There was no game planned. It was for a story I'm writing called &quot;<a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/12724034/1/Of-Duty-and-Love\" target=\"_blank\">Of Duty and Love</a>&quot; It centers around a changeling named Erik, heading out to save the adopted child of his fetch. His story starts in new Orleans but will move to Salt Lake City, where his Fetch lives. Where his &quot;niece&quot; is being held captive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 11-21-2017, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T21:34:03-08:00","id":1161084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1155727-choosing-a-city-for-a-chronicles-of-darkness-game?p=1155878#post1155878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying that Chicago is going to be about mobsters is like saying Portland would be about getting Shanghai\u2019d. Look to modern events and strange happenings, not whatever was going on a century ago for a brief decade.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know Portland Oregon has a serious human trafficking problem to this day, right? <br /> <br /> Real life tragedy google: human trafficking portland oregon<br /> <br /> Side note doesn't Chicago have a Freehold write up about it being the windy blow hard city of rumor mongering in the play test?<br /> <br /> Also congratulations on a solution that get more than one city. Nice call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-21-2017, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}